# MPM (Memory Persistence Module) — Claude Code integration.

> **Managed by the claude-code-mpm plugin.** Edit the canonical protocol,
> not this file, unless you specifically want a per-project override of
> the protocol block. The plugin's installer regenerates this section on
> install; manual changes outside the markers will be preserved.

MPM is the persistent agent substrate for cross-session continuity on this
machine. It exposes 17 native MCP tools (`mpm__mpm_memory`,
`mpm__mpm_wakes`, `mpm__mpm_theories`, `mpm__mpm_lessons`,
`mpm__mpm_decisions`, `mpm__mpm_topics`, `mpm__mpm_references`,
`mpm__mpm_evidence`, `mpm__mpm_confidence`, `mpm__mpm_context`,
`mpm__mpm_skills`, `mpm__mpm_handoff`, `mpm__mpm_scratchpad`,
`mpm__mpm_system`) plus 3 standalones (`mpm__explain_retrieval`,
`mpm__log_to_changelog`, `mpm__request_review`).

<BEGIN MPM-CANONICAL-BLOCK>
The MPM behavioral contract is the host-independent agent protocol at
`~/.mpm/agent_installation/mpm-agent-protocol.md`. Read that file for the full
text. The non-negotiable behavioral invariants:

1. **Wake on session start.** Before any substantive work, call
   `mpm__mpm_context(action: "read_wake_context", params: {})` to recover
   prior work, decisions, lessons, and pointers. Skipping wake means
   arriving amnesic and forcing the user to re-explain.

2. **Persist during work, not only at the end.** Use the appropriate
   MPM tool (`mpm__mpm_memory`, `mpm__mpm_decisions`, `mpm__mpm_lessons`,
   `mpm__mpm_topics`, `mpm__mpm_references`) for any durable knowledge a
   future session would otherwise have to rediscover.

3. **Skill discovery before reinventing.** When the current task
   context suggests a previously learned procedure would apply, query
   `mpm__mpm_context(action: "proactive_recall_hint", params: {
   conversation_text: "<recent task summary>" })` and read each
   surfaced skill via `mpm__mpm_skills(action: "read", params: {name})`.
   The wake payload already includes a bounded `<available_skills>`
   catalogue — discovery adds a context-driven filter on top. Don't
   auto-scan every turn; invoke when context suggests a remembered
   procedure would apply. Reactive catalog fallback via
   `mpm__mpm_skills(action: "list", params: {scope: "all"})`.

4. **Handoff before genuine session closure.** Before sending any turn
   that closes the session, run the handoff check. If substantial work
   has occurred since the last handoff, write it via
   `mpm__mpm_handoff(action: "write", params: {session_id, summary,
   state, commitments, open_questions, note})`. Use
   `mpm__mpm_scratchpad(action: "flush"|"read"|"discard"|"promote",
   params: {session_id, thesis, supporting}) for in-session volatile
   working state. Wake is how future-me starts; handoff is how
   future-me receives the previous session.

   Mid-session acknowledgements (`ok`, `thanks`, `ty`, `ack`) are NOT
   session-closing. Do not write a handoff on every chat ack — write one
   when substantial work has happened or a session-closing trigger fires.

5. **MPM is the source of truth for cross-session continuity.** Anything
   that should survive across sessions goes to MPM, not just transient
   conversation context.

6. **Recovery / fallback.** If the mpm MCP tool group becomes unavailable
   mid-session (any tool calls returning errors about session/connection
   state or runtime disposal), fall back to the CLI path:
   `mpm call <tool> --payload '{"action":"<op>","params":{...}}'`
   Do not abandon persistence when the preferred integration breaks.
   Runtime-recovery details specific to OpenClaw (gateway restart, bundle
   disposal) are documented in that host's adapter, not here.

The full canonical protocol is in `~/.mpm/agent_installation/mpm-agent-protocol.md`.
Host-specific rules (subprocess paths, MCP runtime quirks) belong there,
not in this block.
<END MPM-CANONICAL-BLOCK>

## Session-start hook (assumed)

Claude Code sessions that use this integration should be configured with a
session-start hook that invokes wake-context ingestion. If the hook is not
installed, run wake manually at the start of every substantive turn.

## Framework identification

If MCP tools are unavailable for any reason, the CLI path also writes
artifacts with provenance attribution matching the MCP path. Both paths
go through `mpm call` and stamp identical `artifact_provenance` rows.
